     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Comparing only the last digits: 2,999 is **less** than 3,000, even though 9 is more than 0.\n- Rounding the wrong way when the digit is 5: **5 goes up**, so 250 rounds to 300 (nearest hundred).\n- Changing the digits on the left when you should keep them: rounding 4,352 to the nearest hundred gives 4,400, not 5,400."
